        rules: {
          objective: 'Profit across phases by winning stock bid value lines, ruff vie pot, set declarations, and trick-stage point settlement.',
          gameplay: 'A hand proceeds in four main stages: (1) bid for right to use stock; highest bidder pays bid amount split to opponents and exchanges by discarding and taking stock cards; (2) vie for Ruff, the highest valued suit total in hand (aces 11, courts 10, numerals face value), with betting actions similar to poker; (3) declare Mournivals (four of a kind) and Gleeks (three of a kind) for fixed payments from opponents; (4) play 12 tricks, eldest leading first trick, following suit when possible, with trump from turn-up card. Trick stage adds point settlement around trick count and honour values. Historical sources disagree on some details, so rule variants must be table-agreed before play.',
          keyRules: [
            'A gleek is three of a kind and a mournival is four of a kind.',
            'Ruff compares best suit-point total, not generic hand rank.',
            'Trick phase is fixed at 12 tricks with follow-suit requirement.',
            'Extant reconstructions differ on specific edge rules; session must declare which reconstruction is authoritative.',
          ],
          hasPlaceholders: false,
        },
        strategy: {
          basic: 'Preserve coherent suit concentration for Ruff while avoiding overpaying in stock bid stage.',
          intermediate: 'Estimate whether stock exchange can materially improve ruff or declaration equity before committing bid money.',
          advanced: 'Coordinate ruff-vie pressure with likely declaration payouts and expected trick-stage honour conversion.',
          tips: [
            'Do not treat stock and ruff stages independently; both consume stake and shape later trick value.',
            "Before play, lock the table's interpretation of disputed historical details to avoid settlement disputes.",
          ],
